    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0141" n="67" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg67"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4787</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Sofia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-10T22:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 10, 1917, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 19, 3.35 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Audience with Minister for Foreign Affairs Wednesday. Received assurances that
                    there would be no break in relations happily existing between the two countries.
                    German-Austrian pressure is still very great but up to date has failed. Official
                    circles in Bulgaria strongly in favor of friendly relations, public sentiment
                    likewise. Newspaper reports of disturbances in Bulgaria entirely unfounded.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
